The paper aims to challenge the conventional assumption that large language models require substantial resources to achieve state-of-the-art performance. By introducing InkubaLM, the authors hope to encourage research and development on low-resource languages, which can lead to improved language access and education in Africa.

The model and datasets are publicly available, making it possible for researchers to build upon this work and contribute to the development of more effective language models for low-resource languages.
